From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Eggleston <eggnet@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 19:27:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Follow the presentation owner for the toplevel
 carrier.

Without window contents, a toplevel shows a carrier: a single opaque pixel
while a full-size client surface covers it from above, or a transparent
full-size buffer that lets client surfaces below it show through.
wayland_client_surface_attach_info() chose it from the stacking of the client
surface being attached, which was enough while a window had a single client
surface. Since the presenter coordination of 0026 and 0027, a window can have
several, and only its presentation owner stacks above the parent.
client_surfaces_attach_info() attaches the native background presenters first
and the owner last, on every present of the owner, so each attach of a
background presenter replaced the owner's opaque carrier with a newly
allocated transparent one, and the owner's attach put an opaque one back.

Warhammer Survivors (Unity 6, D3D11 through DXVK) gets there in exclusive
fullscreen after Alt+Tab, once the retired presenter has been promoted
(winewayland-promote-retired-presenter-when-owner-stops-presenting.patch): the
swapchain that owned the window while it came back stays alive and idle. Two
3840x2160 transparent buffers were then allocated, cleared and committed on
every frame, about 9 ms per frame, and the game dropped from 90 to 68 frames
per second and reacted to the mouse visibly late until it quit.

Choose the carrier from the toplevel's presentation owner, as
wayland_surface_update_hwnd_dmabufs() already does, and keep the opaque
carrier when a background presenter detaches while the owner covers the
toplevel.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c | 24 +++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
index 65fa51bf64f..b091922a0b2 100644
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
@@ -5157,6 +5157,23 @@ static void wayland_client_surface_cancel_frame_callback(struct wayland_client_s
     if (client->throttle) NtSetEvent(client->throttle, NULL);
 }
 
+/* The carrier belongs to the toplevel surface, which all the client surfaces
+ * attached to it share. Follow the toplevel's presentation owner, as
+ * wayland_surface_update_hwnd_dmabufs() does: with several presenters on a
+ * window, a background presenter would otherwise replace the owner's opaque
+ * carrier with a transparent one on every attach, and the owner would put the
+ * opaque one back. */
+static BOOL wayland_client_surface_carrier_opaque(struct wayland_win_data *toplevel_data,
+                                                  struct wayland_surface *surface,
+                                                  struct wayland_client_surface *client,
+                                                  BOOL stack_above_parent)
+{
+    struct wayland_client_surface *owner = toplevel_data->client_surface;
+
+    if (!owner || owner == client) return stack_above_parent;
+    return owner->stack_above_parent && owner->toplevel_wl_surface == surface->wl_surface;
+}
+
 void wayland_client_surface_attach(struct wayland_client_surface *client, HWND toplevel)
 {
     struct wayland_win_data *toplevel_data;
@@ -5185,11 +5202,12 @@ void wayland_client_surface_attach(struct wayland_client_surface *client, HWND t
         client->toplevel = 0;
         client->stack_above_parent = FALSE;
 
-        /* An opaque carrier is only valid while its full-size client covers it. */
+        /* An opaque carrier is only valid while the owner's full-size client covers it. */
         if (previous_toplevel && (toplevel_data = wayland_win_data_get(previous_toplevel)))
         {
             surface = toplevel_data->wayland_surface;
-            if (surface && surface->carrier_attached && surface->carrier_opaque)
+            if (surface && surface->carrier_attached && surface->carrier_opaque &&
+                !wayland_client_surface_carrier_opaque(toplevel_data, surface, client, FALSE))
                 wayland_surface_attach_transparent_carrier(surface);
             wayland_win_data_release(toplevel_data);
         }
@@ -5272,7 +5290,7 @@ void wayland_client_surface_attach(struct wayland_client_surface *client, HWND t
 
     if (!toplevel_data->window_contents)
     {
-        if (stack_above_parent)
+        if (wayland_client_surface_carrier_opaque(toplevel_data, surface, client, stack_above_parent))
             wayland_surface_attach_opaque_carrier(surface);
         else
             wayland_surface_attach_transparent_carrier(surface);
